/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  curate24_vp_dimethylSulfoxide -- the vapour pressure of dimethylSulfoxide, REFITTED to
  measurements (DEV.md 4c C281 step 2).  Written by `bin/choupo-curate vp
  dimethylSulfoxide`; everything above the RESULT paragraph is the DECLARATION, committed
  before any fit ran, so it can be read against the result.

  WHY.  The catalogue record carried `vaporPressure { model AmbroseWalton; }`,
  a corresponding-states ESTIMATE from Tc, Pc and omega that never reads the
  record's own Tb (C279 measured a median 19.6 % AAD over the 25 such records
  with archive data).  Here a three-parameter Antoine is fitted to ONE
  laboratory and held out on ANOTHER that shares no author with it.

  STUDIES (one per article, extracted by `choupo-thermoml extract-vp`; ranked
  by points, ties by DOI):
      10.1016/j.fluid.2011.02.002      21 pts  293.15-308.16 K  Fulem; Ruzicka; Ruzicka
      10.1021/je400531a                19 pts  401.95-463.45 K  Zhang; Lv; Huang; Jia et al.
      10.1016/j.jct.2018.04.014         9 pts  353.1-433.1 K  de Pablo; Segovia; Martin; Martin et al.
  SET ASIDE BY NAME:
      10.1016/j.fluid.2007.08.001: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1016/j.jct.2007.04.004: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1016/j.jct.2018.12.016: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1016/j.jct.2019.03.036: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/acs.jced.6b00040: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/acs.jced.6b00733: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/je700408x: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5

  PARTITION (the C16 rule, declared): FIT = the study with the most points,
  doi 10.1016/j.fluid.2011.02.002 (21 pts, 293.15-308.16 K); HELD OUT =
  the next largest sharing no author with it, doi 10.1021/je400531a (19 pts,
  401.95-463.45 K).

  BAND: maxAAD 3.2 % (declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 19 points (1.02 to 6.54 %, mean 3.128 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean).

  NORMAL BOILING POINT: the record's Tb 462.15 K lies INSIDE the measured span 293.15-463.45 K: the held-out verdict is the test there, no further condition.

  NO MEASURED POINT IS IN THIS TREE: constant/archiveDatasets declares both
  series by DOI, NIST URL and sha256; `bin/choupo-curate fetch` regenerates
  them into constant/archiveExtracts/ (gitignored).

  RESULT
  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  (filled in by bin/choupo-curate after the run)
  @@RESULT-END@@
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name       fit_antoine;
        type       vaporPressureFit;
        component  dimethylSulfoxide;

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/dimethylSulfoxide-vapourPressure-j.fluid.2011.02.002.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1016/j.fluid.2011.02.002"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/dimethylSulfoxide-vapourPressure-je400531a.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/je400531a"; }
                role      validation;
            }
        );

        acceptance
        {
            maxAAD  3.2 percent;
            origin  "declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 19 points (1.02 to 6.54 %, mean 3.128 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean";
        }

        output     { file fit_antoine.csv; }
    }
);
